                <pb facs="0451" n="417" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg417"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sherman to Mr. Baker.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-04-03"><hi rendition="#italic">April 3,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Maritime Canal Company apprehends Nicaraguan Government may declare concession
                    forfeited. As concession does not expire until October, 1899, yon are instructed
                    to watch carefully, and if such intention appear, interpose discreet
                    remonstrances for protection of rights of this American corporation, promptly
                    reporting your action.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sherman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
